ps://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.7 dev3 at least and up.\nNot Reproducible in 4.6 Stable and below.\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.dev4 - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5060 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9144) - AMD Ryzen 5 3600 6-Core Processor (12 threads) - 15.94 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nHi,\nNew to this bug report thing so let me know if I missed anything.\nI have a Control scene in my game that has some kind of issue with the ViewportTexture. If this viewport is ever rendered on screen, the entire engine crashes. It occurs during game run and in editor, without printing a stack trace or error. I'm not sure what's causing it, or why, beyond that it seems to occur in a few different scenes, it doesn't occur in versions 4.6 stable or below, and that it happens every single time without fail. It seems to have something to do with how the viewport is rendered, but beyond that, I don't know. \n\nI've included what is essentially my game completely cut down to only include this primary scene that I first discovered the issue on, and the scene that used this problem scene in my game, as I wasn't able to find it consistently in some other scenes, or in a new project. My personal guess is that it's something to do with my project settings. Another element to it is that, it didn't seem to happen if the Transparent Background boolean was turned off on the SubViewport?\n\nIt doesn't have anything to do with the actual written code I've done, you don't need to run the project to see this error, so keep that in mind. I've only included the scripts and other extraneous elements to ensure completeness of the scene and preserve it so that the issue continues.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nStep 1: Open the scene \"character_selection_box.tscn\"\nStep 2: Locate the \"scene\" Node3D and place it as a child of the SubViewport node.\nStep 3: Render the SubViewport in it's 2D scene. You can click on the SubViewport to render the preview, render the whole scene by clicking on the 2D button, or run the project.\nStep 4: Enjoy a full editor crash!\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[bloodtroupe-(copy-to-fix-issue).zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26615419/bloodtroupe-.copy-to-fix-issue.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118361/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rock